//     inside a rock "cheek" (the outer parapet rises with the steps, rock blocks hide the support: no masonry wedges);
//   • irregular lava-rock OUTCROPS breaking the fan's ends and strewn over the flank (they collide);
//   • lava seams either side of the fan, pooling at the foot;
//   • the LOOKOUT CRAG: a jointed-block butte SW of the cone (foreground totems, a BANANA CO. crate) with a spiral stair cut
//     against its back faces (solid, no floating slabs).
